# For developers

Bee Box is developed in an unusually agentic way: one maintainer directing
coding agents, with the instructions those agents work from checked into the
repository. The contributor documentation describes that process, the repo
layout, how to run it from source, how tests work, and how a change lands.

{% agent-prompt title="Work on the code" id="develop-with-your-agent" %}
```
Read https://beebox.run/llms-dev.txt and follow its links as needed. I'm
going to work on the Bee Box codebase; answer my questions from those pages.
```
{% /agent-prompt %}

Reading it yourself: start at
[CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/ianb/beebox/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)
in the repository, or the [contributor entry point](https://beebox.run/llms-dev.txt).
Bug reports are invited; pull requests are not yet solicited.
